          }
        ],
        "conclusion": "There exist C>0 and tau0>0, depending only on T,gamma,R, such that for every real mean-zero u0 in H^gamma(Torus) with ||u0||_(H^gamma)<=R and every positive integer L with tau=T/L<=tau0, the exact solution u and the fixed unfiltered scheme U defined below satisfy max_{0<=n<=L} ||u(n*tau)-U^n||_2 <= C*tau^gamma. The exact solution is the unique real mean-zero C([0,T];H^gamma) distributional solution obtained by smooth approximation. Both constants are uniform over the entire initial-data ball, all such L, and Fourier support."
